@startuml dispatch_dedup_and_output_frames
allowmixing
title Dispatch dedup + output_frames + async failure flow\n(class diagram of changes)

skinparam classFontSize 11
skinparam noteFontSize 10
skinparam classBackgroundColor<<NEW>> #DCFCE7
skinparam classBackgroundColor<<CHANGED>> #FEF3C7
skinparam classBackgroundColor<<DELETED>> #FEE2E2

' =====================================================================
' API layer
' =====================================================================

package "api/routers" {
  class JobsRouter <<CHANGED>> {
    + POST /agent-failure
    + POST /register-outputs
  }
  note right of JobsRouter
    **CHANGED**:
    /agent-failure now takes
    BackgroundTasks; returns
    **202** immediately and
    runs CallbackRouter.route
    in background.
    Agent no longer blocks
    on the orchestration chain.
  end note

  class InternalRouter <<CHANGED>> {
    + POST /internal/orphan/{job_id}
  }
  note right of InternalRouter
    **CHANGED**: same
    BackgroundTasks pattern.
    backup_monitor cron
    doesn't block either.
  end note
}

' =====================================================================
' Callbacks layer
' =====================================================================

class CallbackRouter {
  + route(job_id, outcome, error)
}
note right of CallbackRouter
  Unchanged.  Still funnels
  SUCCESS / FAILURE through
  is_job_terminal short-circuit
  + handler dispatch.
end note

JobsRouter --> CallbackRouter : background.add_task
InternalRouter --> CallbackRouter : background.add_task

' =====================================================================
' Orchestration layer
' =====================================================================

package "orchestrator" {
  class RenderLifecycle <<CHANGED>> {
    + handle_chunk_failed(job_id, error)
    + _try_dispatch_retry(job_id, error)
    + _write_terminal_snapshot(...)
  }
  note right of RenderLifecycle
    **CHANGED — handle_chunk_failed**:
    First call now is
    in_progress.release_if_owner(...).
    If False (lost the race) →
    mark_failed + return.
    Atomic dedup point.

    **CHANGED — _try_dispatch_retry**:
    Optimistic stale-signal guard
    REMOVED (lines 328-334).
    release_if_owner replaces it.

    **CHANGED — _write_terminal_snapshot**:
    Reads count_for_group and
    list_for_group from
    OutputFrameRepository
    instead of parsing JSON
    output_files per job.
  end note

  class DispatchCoordinator <<CHANGED>> {
    + enqueue_and_flush(group_id, tasks, ctx)
  }
  note right of DispatchCoordinator
    **CHANGED**:
    Before each queue_repo.enqueue,
    checks
    in_progress.current_job_for(
      group_id, chunk_index).
    If non-None → skip enqueue.
    Belt-and-suspenders for any
    caller that forgot to release.
  end note

  class LifecycleFramesDeduplication <<DELETED>> {
    DELETED
  }
  note right of LifecycleFramesDeduplication
    **DELETED entirely**.
    Set-union dedup over
    jobs.output_files JSON
    is gone — replaced by
    DB-level uniqueness
    on output_frames.
  end note
}

CallbackRouter --> RenderLifecycle : handle_chunk_failed
RenderLifecycle --> DispatchCoordinator : enqueue_and_flush

' =====================================================================
' Service layer
' =====================================================================

package "services" {
  class JobService <<CHANGED>> {
    + register_outputs(job_id, files)
  }
  note right of JobService
    **CHANGED — register_outputs**:
    Calls
    output_frame_repo.add_many(...)
    instead of jobs.merge_output_files.
    Sibling retries that uploaded
    the same frame are deduped by
    the PK (group_id, filename) at
    INSERT time.
  end note

  class RenderGroupService <<CHANGED>> {
  }
  note right of RenderGroupService
    **CHANGED**:
    available_output_files_count
    now from
    output_frame_repo.count_for_group(group_id)
    not from summing tasks.
  end note

  class RenderGroupSerializer <<CHANGED>> {
    + serialize(group, jobs)
  }
  note right of RenderGroupSerializer
    **CHANGED**:
    Was a pure module.
    Becomes a class, with
    OutputFrameRepository
    injected.  Per-task
    output_files / count /
    latest read via
    list_for_job(job_id).
  end note

  class OutputsResolver <<CHANGED>> {
  }
  note right of OutputsResolver
    **CHANGED**:
    list_for_job(job_id) instead
    of parsing JSON column.
  end note
}

JobService --> JobsRouter
RenderGroupService --> RenderGroupSerializer

' =====================================================================
' Repositories
' =====================================================================

package "repositories" {

  class InProgressChunkRepository <<CHANGED>> {
    + claim_or_replace(...)
    + current_job_for(...)
    + release(...)
    + release_all(...)
    + release_if_owner(\n  group_id, chunk_index,\n  expected_job_id) : bool
  }
  note right of InProgressChunkRepository
    **NEW METHOD — release_if_owner**:
    DELETE FROM in_progress_chunks
     WHERE group_id      = ?
       AND chunk_index   = ?
       AND current_job_id = ?
    RETURNING current_job_id

    Atomic.  Only ONE concurrent
    caller gets a row back; others
    see 0 rows and bail.
    THIS is the dedup mechanism.
  end note

  class DispatchQueueRepository <<CHANGED>> {
    + enqueue(group_id, item)
    + dequeue_for_fleet(fleet)
    + drain(group_id)
  }
  note right of DispatchQueueRepository
    **CHANGED — enqueue**:
    INSERT … ON CONFLICT
    (group_id, chunk_index)
    DO NOTHING.
    DB-level safety net for any
    race that slips past the
    coordinator's app-level check.

    **QueueItem.chunk_index**:
    no longer Optional — schema
    column flips to NOT NULL.
  end note

  class JobRepository <<CHANGED>> {
    + get_raw_by_id(...)
    + mark_failed(...)
    + count_active_by_fleet()
  }
  note right of JobRepository
    **DELETED methods**:
    • get_output_files
    • merge_output_files

    **CHANGED**: INSERT statements
    no longer write the
    output_files column.
  end note

  class OutputFrameRepository <<NEW>> {
    + add_many(group_id, job_id,\n    files) : list[str]
    + count_for_group(group_id) : int
    + count_for_job(job_id) : int
    + list_for_group(group_id) : list[str]
    + list_for_job(job_id) : list[str]
    + unique_filenames_for_chunk(\n    group_id, chunk_index) : set[str]
  }
  note right of OutputFrameRepository
    **NEW REPOSITORY**.
    Single source of truth for
    output frames.

    add_many uses ON CONFLICT
    (group_id, filename) DO
    NOTHING RETURNING filename.
    Returns the rows actually
    inserted — empty list means
    a sibling already uploaded
    every frame in this batch.
  end note

  class JobCounts <<CHANGED>> {
    + uploaded : int
  }
  note right of JobCounts
    **CHANGED**:
    uploaded → count_for_job.
  end note
}

RenderLifecycle --> InProgressChunkRepository : release_if_owner\n_write_terminal_snapshot
DispatchCoordinator --> InProgressChunkRepository : current_job_for
DispatchCoordinator --> DispatchQueueRepository : enqueue / dequeue
JobService --> OutputFrameRepository : add_many
RenderGroupService --> OutputFrameRepository : count_for_group
RenderGroupSerializer --> OutputFrameRepository : list_for_job
OutputsResolver --> OutputFrameRepository : list_for_job
JobCounts --> OutputFrameRepository : count_for_job
RenderLifecycle --> OutputFrameRepository : count_for_group / list_for_group

